  message: "DONE. Annotated the 9 OPEN cohort members against ADR-0051's axiom (tags `axis` + `module_key`; ONE discussion entry each naming the clause violated and the notion the slot carries):\n  INV-linub  sentinel -- the class, read from the consumer side (\"not a marker for the absence of an answer\")\n  INV-kotob  receiver_variable (\"not the receiver's variable name\"; s2 is this item as principle)\n  INV-mumov  sentinel (attribute-chain receiver; L3 instance of the class)\n  INV-papih  sentinel + the owner path displaced into the NAME slot (audit Pair 3; rust's INV-januj)\n  WI-sugom   namespace truncated one segment; the owning submodule in the NAME slot (Pair 3)\n  WI-gudak   receiver_variable, varying per edge under one symbol id\n  WI-papar   sentinel; the inferred TYPE computed and dropped before the slot\n  WI-kamin   type, package-STRIPPED -- the spelling clause; why the naive carry hijacks\n  WI-monul   consumer side: the remedy s2 names (receiver_type_hint unread at the seam)\nTally: sentinel 4, receiver_variable 2, owner path mis-spelled 2, consumer-side 1. The pile is dominated by \"the owner path was known or knowable and the slot got the sentinel\" -- INV-linub's class statement and WI-monul's remedy, which is the legibility this item was for.\n\nNOT annotated -- already closed when swept (each re-read, per this item's STATUS CARE; never isbefore onto a satisfied item): INV-zuvib, INV-hahak, INV-fofoj, INV-januj, INV-safig, INV-fokik, INV-funuf, INV-zimud, INV-dijor (satisfied); WI-zazul, WI-damir (done). Nothing folded, closed, or re-prioritised; folds are the human's per the tracker-hygiene playbook."  # a348
